el against <italic>Schistosoma mansoni</italic> is dependent on host antibody response.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>139</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3108397</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000350-AlKadi1"><label>46</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>AlKadi</surname><given-names>HO</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Antimalarial drug toxicity: a review.</article-title><source>Chemotherapy</source><volume>53</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>391</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17934257</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000350-Pham1"><label>47</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pham</surname><given-names>YT</given-names></name><name><surname>Nosten</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Farinotti</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gimenez</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Cerebral uptake of mefloquine enantiomers in fatal cerebral malaria.</article-title><source>Int J Clin Pharmacol Ther</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>58</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10027484</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000350-Peters1"><label>48</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mittelholzer</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Crevoisier</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturchler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>The chemotherapy of rodent malaria. LII. Response of <italic>P